# An overflow raises where it happens, even when a later step would bring the
# value back into range: `greatest + 1 - 1` never reaches `- 1`. Subtle because
# the exact value of the whole expression is in range.
#= {
#=     raises: 'Int overflow: 9223372036854775807 + 1',
#=     inputs: {greatest: 9223372036854775807},
#= }
def {greatest} = import('inputs')
greatest + 1 - 1
